IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sfa-core`
IMPORT `sfa-periods`

-- Securities and Futures Act 2001 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, SSO informal consolidation (a rendering, not the official text).
-- Layer 1, part sfad: Part 13 Division 1 Subdivision (5), s 282AA, "Power of Authority to issue directions" (lines 44990-45042 of SFA2001.txt).
-- Imports prelude, daydate, sfa-core and sfa-periods (no period is counted in this section; the imports are the house header).
--
-- How to read a function in this module: as in sfad-nocons-small-private.l4 (JUST TRUE yes; JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words; NOTHING where it does not say).
--   Subsection (1) gives the Authority a power to direct three kinds of recipient; each paragraph is its own function and the function for subsection (1)
--   takes the answers of the paragraphs. Subsection (2) is a duty on the person given the notice and is also a regulative rule (no time limit, so no trace reaches BREACH).
--   "-- FORK" lines are collected into the fork register of NOTES.md.

§ `s 282AA(1): the Authority's power to issue directions`

-- src:44999 | (a) to a person making an offer of securities, being an offer
-- src:45000 | made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile
-- src:45001 | statement or an offer referred to in section 280, on
-- src:45002 | matters in connection with the offer;
@ref s 282AA(1)(a) (src:44999-45002)
GIVEN
    `the direction is to a person making an offer of securities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the direction to a person making an offer of securities?
    `the offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement?
    `the offer is an offer referred to in section 280` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the offer an offer referred to in section 280 (an offer made using an automated teller machine or other prescribed electronic means)? (Pass what the function for section 280(1) "the offer is an offer referred to in section 280" answers.)
    `the direction is on matters in connection with the offer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the direction on matters in connection with the offer?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282AA(1)(a) the direction is to a person making an offer of securities, on matters in connection with the offer` MEANS
    IF `the direction is to a person making an offer of securities` AND (`the offer is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement` OR `the offer is an offer referred to in section 280`) AND `the direction is on matters in connection with the offer`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person making an offer of securities, being an offer made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement or an offer referred to in section 280, on matters in connection with the offer"

-- src:45004 | (b) to a person referred to in paragraph (a) who is a borrowing
-- src:45005 | entity, on matters in connection with the requirements and
-- src:45006 | obligations under Subdivision (3) of this Division, in
-- src:45007 | addition to the matters referred to in paragraph (a); or
@ref s 282AA(1)(b) (src:45004-45007)
GIVEN
    `the person is a person referred to in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person one referred to in section 282AA(1)(a) (a person making an offer of securities that is made in or accompanied by a prospectus or profile statement, or an offer referred to in section 280)?
    `the person is a borrowing entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a borrowing entity?
    `the direction is on matters in connection with the requirements and obligations under Subdivision (3) of this Division` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the direction on matters in connection with the requirements and obligations under Subdivision (3) of Division 1 of Part 13 (debentures)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282AA(1)(b) the direction is to a borrowing entity, on matters in connection with the requirements and obligations of Subdivision (3)` MEANS
    IF `the person is a person referred to in paragraph (a)` AND `the person is a borrowing entity` AND `the direction is on matters in connection with the requirements and obligations under Subdivision (3) of this Division`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a person referred to in paragraph (a) who is a borrowing entity, on matters in connection with the requirements and obligations under Subdivision (3) of this Division"

-- src:45009 | (c) to a trustee appointed under section 265A(1).
@ref s 282AA(1)(c) (src:45009-45009)
GIVEN
    `the direction is to a trustee appointed under section 265A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the direction to a trustee appointed under section 265A(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282AA(1)(c) the direction is to a trustee appointed under section 265A(1)` MEANS
    IF `the direction is to a trustee appointed under section 265A(1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "to a trustee appointed under section 265A(1)"

-- src:44994 | 282AA.—(1) The Authority may, where it thinks it necessary or
-- src:44995 | expedient in the interests of the public or a section of the public or for
-- src:44996 | the protection of investors, issue directions, whether of a general or
-- src:44997 | specific nature, by written notice —
@ref s 282AA(1) (src:44994-44997)
GIVEN
    `the Authority thinks it necessary or expedient in the interests of the public or a section of the public or for the protection of investors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the Authority think it necessary or expedient, in the interests of the public or a section of the public or for the protection of investors, to issue the direction?
    `the direction is issued by written notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the direction issued by written notice?
    `the answer of paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 282AA(1)(a) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 282AA(1)(b) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
    `the answer of paragraph (c)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN @desc What does the function for section 282AA(1)(c) answer? Pass NOTHING if you do not know.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282AA(1) the Authority may issue the direction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the Authority thinks it necessary or expedient in the interests of the public or a section of the public or for the protection of investors` AND `the direction is issued by written notice`)
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "The Authority may, where it thinks it necessary or expedient in the interests of the public or a section of the public or for the protection of investors, issue directions"  -- SPLIT-SITE (ii)
        IF (`the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the answer of paragraph (c)` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "whether of a general or specific nature, by written notice"
    -- FORK s282AA-1 | s 282AA(1) | `s 282AA(1) the Authority may issue the direction` | took NOTHING where the Authority does not think the direction necessary or expedient, or does not give it by written notice: the gate "where it thinks it necessary or expedient" is the Authority's own opinion, a standard for exercising its power, not a fact the caller can show to be absent, and the text does not say what the Authority may do when it holds no such view | other reading JUST FALSE (the text says "where", and the periods ruling's item (b) says a failed "where" condition answers JUST FALSE) | licence the grant ruling's limit 1 ({G1}: NOTHING for a power whose gate failed; the "In short" sentence: "limits a grant or prohibition in its own wording and the case falls outside the limit"); {G3} says to list a "may" function whose gate is "where" and not to change it: this is a split site (ii) of the brief, answered as at section 281(1) (the gate is the Authority's own state of mind) and unlike sections 277(1AB), (1AD) and (2) (an application or a declaration the caller can show absent). Listed under the marginal readings.
    -- FORK s282AA-1p | s 282AA(1)(a), (b) and (c) | the three paragraph functions | took NOTHING for a recipient outside the paragraph (the paragraphs name the persons to whom the Authority may issue directions and do not say it may not direct anyone else) | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {P-c} (a scope limit with no "only") and {G1}

§ `s 282AA(2) to (5): the duty to comply, publication, the offence and the trustee's immunity`

-- src:45013 | (2) Any person to whom a notice is given under subsection (1) must
-- src:45014 | comply with every direction contained in the notice.
@ref s 282AA(2) (src:45013-45014)
GIVEN
    `a notice is given to the person under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has a notice been given to the person under section 282AA(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282AA(2) the person given the notice must comply with every direction contained in it` MEANS
    IF `a notice is given to the person under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person to whom a notice is given under subsection (1) must comply with every direction contained in the notice"
    -- FORK s282AA-2 | s 282AA(2) | `s 282AA(2) the person given the notice must comply with every direction contained in it` | took JUST FALSE for a person to whom no notice is given (the duty is the person's own question, and it is a duty) | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} (keep JUST FALSE "for a bar, a duty or the provision's own question") and {CC} (a duty whose "if" is unmet). The regulative rule below has no time limit: "must comply" gives none, so no trace reaches BREACH (listed under "Rules with no breach path").

-- src:45021 | (3) It is not necessary to publish any direction issued under
-- src:45022 | subsection (1) in the Gazette.
@ref s 282AA(3) (src:45021-45022)
GIVEN
    `the direction is issued under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the direction one issued under section 282AA(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282AA(3) the direction need not be published in the Gazette` MEANS
    IF `the direction is issued under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is not necessary to publish any direction issued under subsection (1) in the Gazette"

-- src:45026 | (4) Any person who contravenes a direction issued to the person
-- src:45027 | under subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence and shall be liable
-- src:45028 | on conviction to a fine not exceeding $50,000 and, in the case of a
-- src:45029 | continuing offence, to a further fine not exceeding $5,000 for every
-- src:45030 | day or part of a day during which the offence continues after
-- src:45031 | conviction.
@ref s 282AA(4) (src:45026-45031)
GIVEN
    `the person contravenes a direction issued to the person under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the person contravene a direction issued to the person under section 282AA(1)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282AA(4) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the person contravenes a direction issued to the person under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Any person who contravenes a direction issued to the person under subsection (1) shall be guilty of an offence"  -- SPLIT-SITE (i)
    -- FORK s282AA-4 | s 282AA(4) | `s 282AA(4) the person is guilty of an offence` | took JUST FALSE where the contravention element is unmet (this provision's own question) | other reading NOTHING | licence {G2} and the brief's split site (i)

@ref s 282AA(4) (src:45026-45031)
GIVETH A Penalty
`s 282AA(4) the penalty for the offence` MEANS Penalty OF 50000, 0, FALSE, 5000

-- src:45035 | (5) No criminal or civil liability shall be incurred by a trustee
-- src:45036 | appointed under section 265A(1), or by any person acting on behalf
-- src:45037 | of such a trustee, for any thing done (including any statement made)
-- src:45038 | or omitted to be done with reasonable care and in good faith in the
-- src:45039 | course of, or in connection with, the compliance or purported
-- src:45040 | compliance with a direction issued to the trustee under subsection (1).
@ref s 282AA(5) (src:45035-45040)
GIVEN
    `the person is a trustee appointed under section 265A(1), or a person acting on behalf of such a trustee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person a trustee appointed under section 265A(1), or a person acting on behalf of such a trustee?
    `the thing was done or omitted in the course of, or in connection with, the compliance or purported compliance with a direction issued to the trustee under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing done (including any statement made) or omitted to be done in the course of, or in connection with, the compliance or purported compliance with a direction issued to the trustee under section 282AA(1)?
    `the thing was done or omitted with reasonable care` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing done or omitted to be done with reasonable care?
    `the thing was done or omitted in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the thing done or omitted to be done in good faith?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 282AA(5) the person incurs no criminal or civil liability for the thing done or omitted` MEANS
    IF `the person is a trustee appointed under section 265A(1), or a person acting on behalf of such a trustee` AND `the thing was done or omitted in the course of, or in connection with, the compliance or purported compliance with a direction issued to the trustee under subsection (1)` AND `the thing was done or omitted with reasonable care` AND `the thing was done or omitted in good faith`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for any thing done (including any statement made) or omitted to be done with reasonable care and in good faith"
    -- FORK s282AA-5 | s 282AA(5) | `s 282AA(5) the person incurs no criminal or civil liability for the thing done or omitted` | took NOTHING where an element is missing (the trustee, the connection with a direction, reasonable care, good faith): the immunity is limited in its own wording and the text does not say that a trustee who lacked care or good faith is liable | other reading JUST FALSE | licence {P-c} (a scope limit with no "only") and {G1}

§ `s 282AA(2): the duty to comply as a regulative rule`

DECLARE `s 282AA party` IS ONE OF
    `s 282AA a person given a notice`

DECLARE `s 282AA act` IS ONE OF
    `s 282AA(2) comply with every direction contained in the notice`

-- src:45013 | (2) Any person to whom a notice is given under subsection (1) must
-- src:45014 | comply with every direction contained in the notice.
@ref s 282AA(2) (src:45013-45014)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 282AA party` `s 282AA act`
`s 282AA(2) the duty to comply with every direction contained in the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `s 282AA a person given a notice`
    MUST `s 282AA(2) comply with every direction contained in the notice`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `s 282AA a person given a notice` BECAUSE "the person did not comply with a direction contained in the notice given under section 282AA(1)"
